{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And every open vessel.</b> The verse speaks of an earthenware vessel, which does not receive impurity from its back but only from its inside. Therefore, if it has no covering pressed and bound tightly upon it, it is impure — but if there is a tightly bound cover upon it, it is pure (there, 25)." "<b>Cord.</b> A term for joined/bound, in Arabic. So too (Genesis 30) ״נַפְתּוּלֵי אֱלֹהִים נִפְתַּלְתִּי״ — I have joined myself with my sister."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:11:38.922513209Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}